WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.539 --> 00:00:03.240
(soft upbeat music)

00:00:03.240 --> 00:00:06.251
- Everybody's got their
favorite part of the cycle.

00:00:06.251 --> 00:00:07.371
There are people that love the wash,

00:00:07.371 --> 00:00:10.349
they love the rinse, or
the spin, or the drain.

00:00:10.349 --> 00:00:11.259
I'm a spin guy.

00:00:11.259 --> 00:00:12.592
I love the spin.

00:00:15.197 --> 00:00:16.808
My name is Jon Charles, and

00:00:16.808 --> 00:00:19.687
I'm a washer collector enthusiast.

00:00:19.687 --> 00:00:20.854
- Laundry day.

00:00:21.699 --> 00:00:24.619
- [Jon] The club got
started around 1987, I think,

00:00:24.619 --> 00:00:28.786
and now we have, like, 3,000
members from all over the world.

00:00:31.717 --> 00:00:33.867
We get together for washes.

00:00:33.867 --> 00:00:35.707
You do laundry 'til like
four in the morning,

00:00:35.707 --> 00:00:38.258
you do your margaritas
and you launder together.

00:00:38.258 --> 00:00:39.091
- To laundry.

00:00:39.091 --> 00:00:40.174
- To laundry.

00:00:41.389 --> 00:00:43.269
- [Jon] We watch the cycles,
you'll see a lot of us

00:00:43.269 --> 00:00:45.528
just stand there and watch
the whole cycle go through.

00:00:45.528 --> 00:00:47.277
- Oh, oh my God.

00:00:47.277 --> 00:00:49.189
- All 3,000 of us come in with a story like

00:00:49.189 --> 00:00:50.467
I thought I was the only one,

00:00:50.467 --> 00:00:54.634
I thought I was the only person
in the world that did this.

00:00:56.029 --> 00:00:58.138
In the collection, I've got 59 machines,

00:00:58.138 --> 00:00:59.829
and I've got 22 hooked up and running

00:00:59.829 --> 00:01:00.908
down here in the basement.

00:01:00.908 --> 00:01:01.909
(knocking)

00:01:01.909 --> 00:01:03.738
I have a good representation of everything

00:01:03.738 --> 00:01:06.571
that was made, from 1938 to today.

00:01:08.309 --> 00:01:10.177
And I take them all apart
and I restore them 'cause

00:01:10.177 --> 00:01:12.587
I wanna know how everything
works inside the machine.

00:01:12.587 --> 00:01:13.928
And then the laundry is for me,

00:01:13.928 --> 00:01:17.345
it's sorta like the frosting on the cake.

00:01:18.848 --> 00:01:20.597
These machines represent a lot of ways

00:01:20.597 --> 00:01:22.677
of doing things in each
decade that changed,

00:01:22.677 --> 00:01:24.688
that we no longer do.

00:01:24.688 --> 00:01:26.498
And I think it's something that should be

00:01:26.498 --> 00:01:28.717
preserved for other people,

00:01:28.717 --> 00:01:31.698
if we can get them interested.

00:01:31.698 --> 00:01:33.018
I just can't go to a cocktail party

00:01:33.018 --> 00:01:34.707
and say, “How's your washer doing?”

00:01:34.707 --> 00:01:36.418
They'd look at me like I was crazy.

00:01:36.418 --> 00:01:37.848
But I can get together with these guys,

00:01:37.848 --> 00:01:40.469
let my hair down, uh, it's just so much fun

00:01:40.469 --> 00:01:42.427
to be able to have a
conversation about it,

00:01:42.427 --> 00:01:44.518
'cause I know laundry's a
chore for everybody else,

00:01:44.518 --> 00:01:46.268
but for us it's play.

